// The legacy pair: SHA-1 and MD5 — present because the world's
// existing data still needs verifying, refused for every security
// purpose. Both are broken: SHA-1 collides by construction since
// 2017, MD5 since 2004; neither answers a new question. One-shot
// only — the streaming surface belongs to the algorithms with a
// future. Digests are raw bytes as String, like the rest of the
// package; render with crypto.hex_encode.

// The SHA-1 digest of data, twenty bytes. Broken for every security
// purpose; for verifying existing data.
def sha1(data String) String {
  return internal.sha1.digest(data)
}

// The MD5 digest of data, sixteen bytes. Broken for every security
// purpose; for verifying existing data.
def md5(data String) String {
  return internal.md5.digest(data)
}
